  ── CONCLUSION ──

  [STRUCTURAL FINDING]
  ChestX6 Normal patient_ids overlap with Emphysema patient_ids: 0
  → Normal and Emphysema subsets in ChestX6 are from COMPLETELY
    SEPARATE patient pools. The naive GroupShuffleSplit placed
    ALL Normal in train and ALL Emphysema in test.
    This structural separation IS itself the primary shortcut.
    Even with real labels, any model that memorizes 'which patient
    pool I'm from' will achieve near-perfect AUC on this split.

  NO SINGLE-DATASET SHORTCUT DETECTED (on stratified splits).
  Both random models failed → Neither dataset alone has a
  shortcut. However, the structural ChestX6 patient-pool
  separation (zero overlap between Normal and Emphysema
  patient IDs) remains a critical confound regardless of AUC.
  The shortcut appears only when datasets are combined in DANN
  — the model learns 'dataset identity' which correlates with
  disease label distribution.

